{:event/body "M0 milestone achieved: (1) CI pre-commit workflow created to block new IStore usage in kotobase.store.* APIs; new imports are rejected while existing code is preserved for incremental migration. (2) Benchmark baseline script (scripts/benchmark-m0-baseline.cljs) established measuring p50/p95/p99 latency, write/read amplification, and CPU cost at 100k datom scale: write p50=13.3ms, read p50=101.7ms, write amplification 5x, read amplification 2.5x (current epoch-flush + novelty hydration + 4-index rebuild pattern). (3) Baseline measurements locked in 90-docs/adr/2607201600-baselines.json as reference point for M1-M6 migration phases. Next: M1 will introduce MerkleRun v1, VersionManifest v1, and pure Block/Head/HeadCAS effect algebra, shadowing current write path and validating equivalence with existing snapshot behavior.", :adr/related ["adr-2607032430-kotoba-datom-log-structured-engine-redesign" "adr-2607032500-kotoba-kotobase-clojure-datomic-relationship"], :adr/id "adr-2607201600-kotobase-merkle-lsm-istore-retirement", :event/summary "M0 phase complete: IStore freeze CI check, benchmark baseline locked", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-20T12:07:05.138Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 10}
{:event/body "2026-07-20 session close. Added the reusable EDN onboarding contract, secret-free GFTD Ads Manager instance record, pure CLJC evaluator, tests, and README guidance under orgs/kotoba-lang/com-googleapis-googleads. Verification: CLJC 4 tests / 8 assertions passed; existing Python adapter 11 tests passed; all three added EDN documents parsed; DataScript query returned the ADR as accepted. Current external state remains brand verification :under-review. Follow-up: poll verification until approved/rejected/action-required and confirm the Google Ads Basic Access application references project gftd-ads-manager rather than the inaccessible legacy project. Repo-wide docs-edn-only verification remains blocked by one unrelated existing non-tx ADR and three unrelated existing .md path references.", :adr/related ["adr-google-ads-oauth-brand-onboarding-edn"], :adr/id "adr-google-ads-oauth-brand-onboarding-edn", :event/summary "Session closed after EDN onboarding abstraction implementation and verification", :event/agent "codex", :event/at "2026-07-20T06:52:25.244Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 11}
{:event/body "手順: (1) orgs/kotoba-lang/browser で npm run compile:smoke → public/visual-smoke.html + public/js/visual-smoke.js(サーバ依存ゼロの自己完結ビルド)。(2) index.htmlへリネームしてWebBundle化(WKURLSchemeHandlerの既定index.html規約に合わせる)。(3) bin/kotoba-shell app scaffold --target macos --manifest-edn '{...:web/dist-dir \"...\"}' → xcodegen成功(placeholder? false、実WebBundleを検出)。(4) bin/kotoba-shell app build --target macos --execute → xcodebuild実ビルド成功(code=app-built)。(5) DerivedDataから実.appを特定しopenで起動、ps確認でPID単一・子プロセス0(Chromeのmulti-process構成とは対照的)。(6) 画面キャプチャで実際にkotoba:dom committed / WebGL host activeという動的ステータス文言(JSがWebGL commit成功後に書き換える値)を確認、静的プレースホルダでないことを確認。既存の :adr/not-decided 「kotoba-shellのmacOSネイティブホスト本実装(WKWebViewによるプラグマティックな実装 or dom-gpu/browser成熟待ちのどちらを採るか)」に対し、WKWebView実用路線を採ったまま:web/dist-dirにdom-gpu/browser自身のR0コンパイル成果物を差し込む、というハイブリッド経路が技術的に動作することを実証した。ただし限界も明確: これはbrowser-demo(WebSocket/Worker/fetch実演、scripts/demo-server.js依存)ではなくvisual-smoke(静的canvas描画のみ)側に限定した検証であり、ネイティブアプリにNodeサーバは同梱していないためデモの動的ネットワーク機能は対象外。またscaffold自体のAppDelegate.swiftは引き続きWKWebViewをハードコードしたままで、dom-gpu/browserを:render-substrateとして選択するCLIフラグが追加されたわけではない(ADR本文が既に明記する既存の設計上の制約は変わらず)。今回の作業はあくまで一回限りの手動検証(:web/dist-dirへの一時ディレクトリ差し込み)であり、shellのデフォルトmanifestやCI gateへの恒久的な組み込みは行っていない。", :adr/related ["2607081015"], :adr/id "adr-2607081015-kotoba-lang-rust-audit-shell-dom-gpu-browser-smoke-gate", :event/summary "kotoba-shell app build --execute で dom-gpu/browser の R0 visual-smoke(WebGL)を:web/dist-dir経由WKWebViewに埋め込み、単一プロセス・Chrome非依存のネイティブmacOSアプリとして実機起動を確認(ADR :not-decided の「macOSネイティブホスト本実装」項への実証データ)。", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-20T07:33:15.327Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 12}
{:event/body "6 real observe->evaluate->decide->act->record-evidence cycles ran (kotoba-lang/loop-system-dynamics ledger has 6 entries). Coverage grew from the original 11 entities to 27 via 4 rounds of new sourced external-reference organizations (Gitcoin, Ethereum Foundation ESP, RadicalxChange, Quakers, Mozilla, Jehovah's Witnesses, Wikimedia, Linux Foundation, GiveWell, global fossil fuel industry, Sardex mutual credit, Optimism RetroPGF, GiveDirectly UBI, online gambling) plus repo-wide breakdowns (cloud-itonami and gftdcojp by name-prefix, west-registered-vs-GitHub-total coverage per org) plus 7 internal com-junkawasaki-ecosystem products connected from the already-existing BMC metrics pipeline (90-docs/business/metrics/*.edn) rather than new research. kotoba-lang/dynamics gained a real statistical function, upper-bound-rate-from-zero-events (the textbook zero-events confidence bound), applied to etzhayyim's own adherent loop: with an estimated ~16,497 unique visitors over etzhayyim.com's ~9 live weeks and zero organic conversions, F2 is now quantified as at most ~0.018% at 95% confidence -- the first actual number for the quantity ADR-2607202800's Step 0 and this ADR's own instrumentation thesis both flagged as the real blocker, rather than an argued-but-unmeasured claim. Structural-strength ranking across all 14 archetypes spans 8+ orders of magnitude (speculative-crypto-derivatives 4.1M down to quaker-consensus-membership 0.025), and a cluster of rigorously-measured real-money charitable/mutual-credit organizations (sardex 1.49, givedirectly-ubi 1.17, givewell 0.85, optimism-retropgf 0.63) converges in the same mid-table band regardless of mechanism (donation, mutual credit, direct cash transfer), suggesting that band is where measurement rigor + moderate self-funding + monthly-to-quarterly cycles land, independent of which specific instrument is used. kotoba-lang's own repo-by-prefix breakdown (1,649 repos: 1,049 com-* vendor-integration specs, 97 kami-* engine, 85 org-* standards specs, 416 actual language/substrate core) shows the org's headline repo count is dominated by passive vendor spec repos, not core substrate work -- a caution against reading raw repo counts as a proxy for active development mass without this breakdown.", :adr/related ["2607202700" "2607202800" "2607202900"], :adr/id "2607203000", :event/summary "6 real iterations landed: 14 loop archetypes, 27 entities, F2 turned from unmeasured to a computed upper bound (<=~0.018% @ 95% confidence)", :event/agent "claude-code", :event/at "2026-07-20T15:42:14.595Z", :event/actor "Jun Kawasaki", :event/type :note, :event/seq 13}
